{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"amoebaean-hemihedral-vervet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nPydantic deliberately counts one Agent-visible model turn even when `FallbackModel` tries multiple candidates inside it. The approved RP-01 decision follows maintained-project practice: keep that request budget authoritative and make candidate activity operationally visible as tracing, not as `candidate_requests` in usage. Current candidate construction is centralized in `model_classes.build_fallback_model` and `runner.PydanticAIRunner` already records ordered candidate provenance (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:414+`, `src/rebar/llm/runner.py:372-465`).\n\n## Approach\nInstrument each already-built fallback or native-to-prompted candidate at the public Pydantic model boundary, preserving the Agent model-request span as the logical-turn parent. Candidate child spans record stable order, provider-qualified model identity, returned or raised outcome, and provider-reported usage when available. Use the existing optional tracing setup, so the base installation stays import-clean and a missing tracing exporter is a no-op. Do not alter `FallbackModel` selection, `ProviderSession` lifecycle, `RunUsage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, or JSONL. Provider SDK/HTTP retries remain outside this candidate layer and are never inferred.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — wrap the concrete candidate models at construction without changing order or fallback predicates.\n- `src/rebar/llm/tracing.py` — define bounded candidate span attributes through the existing optional tracing seam.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — pass candidate order/provenance into instrumentation without adding retry policy.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py` — candidate order, outcome, provenance, and usage non-interference.\n- New focused tracing test module using an in-memory exporter from the existing tracing development dependency.\n\n## Testing\n- Primary 503 then fallback success yields one Agent request and two ordered candidate spans.\n- All candidates fail yields two error spans and the existing ordered `FallbackExceptionGroup`.\n- Native-schema rejection then prompted success yields two candidate spans and one Agent request.\n- Tracing disabled yields identical result, usage, imports, and exception behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Primary-failure/fallback-success emits two ordered candidate spans beneath one logical Agent request span, with the fallback model recorded as the answer; verified by an in-memory exporter test.\n- [ ] All-candidate failure emits one sanitized error outcome per attempted candidate and preserves the existing ordered exception group and resolution classification; verified by fallback-chain tests.\n- [ ] Native-to-prompted downgrade emits native-raised then prompted-returned candidate outcomes without adding an Agent request or changing fallback eligibility; verified by a focused downgrade trace test.\n- [ ] Candidate spans contain no prompt, response, credential, endpoint secret, or unsanitized exception body when content tracing is disabled; verified by secret-canary assertions.\n- [ ] `_usage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, and durable usage JSONL are identical with tracing on and off and contain no candidate counter; verified by paired-result assertions.\n- [ ] Importing and running the base installation without the tracing extra remains successful and creates no span dependency error; verified by the lean-import subprocess test.","id":"2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","tracing"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S4 — Trace fallback and downgrade candidates without redefining usage"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786924755313354001,"uuid":"b0b626b1-5e5c-4658-b27b-43ac1e4c41ac"}